# What a loop that carries a mapped list holds, watched (kanso#2302).
#
# `doubled` answers `list/to_list` of `list/map`. The map is a `mapped`
# record, and `to_list` reads it through `list/fold`, so the answer is a list
# exactly when a call to the fold answers what its init and lambda can. It
# did not before kanso#2321, and this loop kept four arena blocks at twelve
# thousand iterations. It holds one.
#
# Watched, not frozen: regenerate deliberately and say which way it went.
import "std/list"

fn doubled xs
  list/to_list (list/map xs (x -> x * 2 % 251))

pub fn carried u left
  looped [1 2 3] u left (left == 0)

fn looped _ u _ true
  u

fn looped p u left false
  next = doubled u
  looped p next (left - 1) (left - 1 == 0)

pub play = print (carried [1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8] 12000)
